178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (The UNSC is one of the six principal organs of the United Nations, it is entrusted with the primary responsibility of maintaining international peace and security. The UNSC was established under the Charter of the United Nations after the devastation of WW2. What makes the UNSC stand out is its ability to make legally binding decisions - especially while responding to crises and ensuring that threats to peace are addressed swiftly.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (Chapter 5 of the UN Charter entrusts the UNSC with taking action to maintain international peace and security \(Article 24\), making decisions that all member states must comply to \(Article 39\), recommend or decide on actions taken on threats to peace using sanctions, intervention and other actions \(Article 39\), investigate situations that may cause international turmoil \(Article 34\), authorize military activity by member states \(Article 43\), and finally, encourage peaceful resolutions of conflicts \(Article 33\). )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 122 0 R
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
